nu_mono (shared definition)  sup column   2.0860 at x=0.001; at x=1e-3,1e-2,0.1,1: 2.086, 1.788, 1.491, 1.164 -> NO plateau (keeps growing); R at sup 0.611, at x=0.1 0.4365
D verdict: P2-specific constant: RAR column -> 0 at small x (no plateau); nu_mono plateau at small x: False (frozen expectation was that BOTH RAR and nu_mono columns vanish at small x: RAR does; nu_mono does NOT, its monotone repair adds a slowly (log) growing extra acceleration, so its column grows toward small x: WRONG expectation, kept)

